course: dictionary
lesson: 8383
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Rubbery means like rubber. «A cat flea can jump about 30 centimetres ... by storing energy in a rubbery pad» shows the pad is soft and bendy, and it springs back, like a catapult.
explain: «In vinegar it fizzes away over days and leaves a rubbery egg held by its thin skin.» The egg is not hard like a normal egg. Ask: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence: soft and bendy fits, so you have the right one.
explain: Rubbery can also describe food that is tough and chewy in an unpleasant way, often because it was cooked too long. The meaning «legs felt rubbery», meaning weak and wobbly from fear or tiredness, is informal, so it mostly appears in stories. Check the clues around the word each time.
fact: Rubbery means like rubber: soft, bendy or bouncy.
fact: A rubbery material is flexible and springs back when you let it go.
fact: Rubbery food is tough and chewy in an unpleasant way, often because it was cooked too long.
fact: «My legs felt rubbery» means weak and wobbly, from fear or tiredness.
fact: The adjective forms are rubbery, rubberier and rubberiest.
exercise: «A cat flea can jump about 30 centimetres by storing energy in a rubbery pad.» What does rubbery mean here? | Hard and cold like a stone | Loud and noisy | Sticky like wet paint | *Soft, bendy and springy
exercise: «Eggshell ... leaves a rubbery egg held by its thin skin.» What does a rubbery egg feel like? | Hard as a rock | Heavy and full of water | Warm and sweet | *Soft and bendy
exercise: Ella says, «My legs felt rubbery after the race.» What does she mean? | Strong and fast | Stretched and longer | Covered in rubber boots | *Weak and wobbly from tiredness
test: «Chewing gum is a rubbery gum base kneaded with sugar or sweetener and flavour.» What is the gum base like? | Liquid like water | Crunchy like a biscuit | Hard like a stone | *Bendy and soft, like rubber
test: A cook says the squid is rubbery because it was cooked too long. What does she mean? | Sweet and sticky | *Tough and chewy in an unpleasant way | Cool and fresh | Bouncy on purpose, like a ball
exam: Which sentence uses rubbery to mean weak and wobbly? | The rubbery pad sprang back | The eggs were rubbery and overcooked | *My legs felt rubbery after the long run | The gum base was rubbery
